course: dictionary
lesson: 10870
title: Video: a word with two jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Video can be a noun or a verb. As a noun, a video is moving pictures with sound that you watch on a screen, or one recording of something. «Videos that are paid adverts are often marked "ad" or "sponsored", sometimes in small print.» Here videos are things you watch.
explain: As a verb, to video means to record something with a camera or phone. The word changes its ending: video, videos, videoed, videoing. «A girl in Kansas hears in a video that a drop of bleach in water cures colds» uses video as a noun, because she hears something in a video.
explain: Check the words around it. If there is a, the, or an s on the end, it is probably a noun. If someone is doing something with a camera, it is probably a verb. Swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Video is a noun: a video, videos.
fact: Video is also a verb: to video, videoed, videoing, meaning to record with a camera or phone.
fact: «Only watch videos an adult says are okay.» This is a safety rule, so check with an adult first.
fact: «Things in videos can be fake», so ask whether something is true before you believe it.
fact: Useful phrases: watch a video, make a video, video call, video game, music video, on video.
exercise: «Recommendations may push videos that keep people watching, including angry or scary ones.» In this sentence, what is a video? | Sound with no pictures | A type of camera | A game you play with a controller | *Moving pictures with sound that you watch on a screen
exercise: Mia says, «I will video the school play so Grandad can see it.» What does video mean here? | *To record something with a camera or phone | To paint a picture of the stage | To watch a film in a cinema | To sing loudly on stage
exercise: Which phrase means a call where you can see each other on a screen? | *video call | music video | on video | video game
test: «A video of the school play» is an example of which meaning? | Moving pictures with no sound | *A recording of something | A new game to play at break | A kind of school bag
test: Ella says, «I will video the match tomorrow.» What kind of word is video here? | Adverb | Noun | Adjective | *Verb
exam: Which sentence uses video as a noun? | «The girl will video her dog» | «They are videoing now» | «Please video me at the park» | *«She watched a video of her dog playing»
